WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.413
What does Learn leave to you?

2
00:00:01.413 --> 00:00:05.713
The commands make one zone, one
link, one endpoint; in practice,

3
00:00:05.713 --> 00:00:10.700
zones still get created in workload
subscriptions, and records split.

4
00:00:10.700 --> 00:00:13.432
A zone group per endpoint
means an endpoint

5
00:00:13.432 --> 00:00:16.088
without one has no record anybody manages.

6
00:00:16.088 --> 00:00:20.135
"Turn public access off once the
private path works" leaves room

7
00:00:20.135 --> 00:00:23.949
for the private path to work
while the public one stays open.

8
00:00:23.949 --> 00:00:26.668
Key Vault's recommendations are read once,

9
00:00:26.668 --> 00:00:29.463
and a vault created next
quarter misses one.

10
00:00:29.463 --> 00:00:33.637
And nslookup has to run from inside
a network, which the kit can't do.

11
00:00:33.637 --> 00:00:39.140
So the kit checks the records' configuration
every run, and Lab 2 runs nslookup.
